This is to announce the availability of the Scribe Bibliography
Generator -- a software tool developed at Wang Institute of Graduate
Studies by Prof. Susan Gerhart.

The Bibliography Generator (BibGen) is a UNIX tool for producing the
bibliography files that Scribe uses for citations and bibliography
entries.  The usual UNIX skills - text editing, file and directory
handling, program calling - are assumed.  Familiarity with the Scribe
manual is required for significant use or varied bibliography entries.
However, new users of Scribe may find the BibGen helpful in learning
Scribe's data model and styles for bibliographies.

Scribe bibliography files contain templates to be filled in describing
reference materials for papers or for a general bibliography, e.g. for
a report or a course.  The user is prompted for field contents of the
materials.  A help system is provided through which the user can ask
for the definitions of the various entries, get hints on what is
expected, and reuse previous field contents.  The BibGen is intended to
be an easy-to-use, efficient, helpful, standardizing way of preparing
Scribe bibliography files.

To receive a copy of BibGen please send a mail to:

	..!decvax!wivax!distrib        (USENET)
	distrib.wang-inst@csnet-relay  (CSNET)

The following is the information required in your mail:

	(1). Your name
	(2). Your organization
	(3). Your CSNET or USENET address

The User's Manual and the code will be mailed to the net address
indicated in (3).  There is no fee for the BibGen at the present.

